  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v3.2.4-rc.1: closes the duplicate-handshake-destroy SCTP cascade. `Torrent.OnHandshake`'s duplicate-detection no longer calls `Destroy()` on either peer — both wires stay alive and the consumer layer (notably `SpawnDev.ILGPU.P2P.P2PWebRtcBridge`) dedupes by canonical BT peerId. Empirically, on Chrome Stable AND Canary, calling `_pc.Close()` on the loser PC caused Chromium to emit `sctp-failure | User-Initiated Abort | sctpCauseCode=12` on the SURVIVOR's data channel, killing the entire peer-to-peer connection. Both sides observed the cascade. Rationale + verification in commit message.",
